1
00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:00,720
The most important thing is there?.

2
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:07,920
The reason why I'm here
is that I'll protect you!.

3
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:13,077
It's okay, let's go ahead and move on!.

4
00:01:13,160 --> 00:01:16,320
The moon will always come to the moon?.

5
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:19,837
The moon will come to the moon!.

6
00:01:19,920 --> 00:01:22,900
Let's look at the moon?.

7
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:14,580
Whew, good, safe and sound.

8
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:17,620
Yeah, that wore me out, huh?

9
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:21,457
Safe and sound, my butt,
I thought I was gonna die!

10
00:02:21,540 --> 00:02:23,280
What was I supposed to do?

11
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:26,577
You were the one who said we couldn't
use the elevator because we'd get caught.

12
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:27,797
I didn't have a choice.

13
00:02:27,880 --> 00:02:30,117
This doesn't mean, hey,
let's jump down, idiot.

14
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:32,397
You can't slide around like
that square-knocked ship right.

15
00:02:32,480 --> 00:02:33,480
Got it? Right.

16
00:02:33,760 --> 00:02:34,820
Sorry about that.

17
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:36,550
Whatever.

18
00:02:36,633 --> 00:02:38,237
It's fine since we're safe now.

19
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:39,580
Then stop hitting me.

20
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:45,740
However, we might not be safe for long.

21
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:48,580
We won't. Why not? What's wrong?

22
00:02:49,480 --> 00:02:51,656
This island's topography and climate.

23
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:55,777
With this much wind blowing and the
atmospheric pressure falling so rapidly,

24
00:02:55,860 --> 00:02:58,437
there's likely going to
be a typhoon here tonight.

25
00:02:58,520 --> 00:03:00,820
This place is called the City of Water.

26
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:02,170
Think about it.

27
00:03:02,253 --> 00:03:04,817
Its greatest weakness
would have to be flooding.

28
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:06,660
Okay, so it floods. So what?

29
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:08,802
Well, it worries me, that's all.

30
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:10,591
I'll check into it later.

31
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:14,095
Come on, let's head back to
the inn for the time being.

32
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:18,497
In compliance with the
Aqua Laguna warning that

33
00:03:18,580 --> 00:03:20,837
was issued for the entire
island earlier today.

34
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:23,317
All docks on the shipbuilding
island are now to be

35
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:26,282
considered public shelter
and evacuation centers.

36
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:31,874
Large crowds are expected, so please
take shelter as quickly as possible.

37
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:37,420
Additionally, keep in mind that Dock
1 is currently in a dangerous state.

38
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:40,198
Alright, I'll put the iron board on.

39
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:44,137
Hey honey, you sure we
have everything we'll need?

40
00:03:44,220 --> 00:03:45,050
Yes.

41
00:03:45,133 --> 00:03:47,437
Now come on, we need to take
shelter in the shipyard.

42
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:48,517
Patience, patience.

43
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:53,177
You gotta be careful sealing this board
if the inside of our house gets flooded,

44
00:03:53,260 --> 00:03:54,497
everything will be ruined.

45
00:03:54,580 --> 00:03:57,737
Hey, the wind is starting to pick up.

46
00:03:57,820 --> 00:04:00,557
The waves will be here anytime now. Hurry.

47
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:05,237
If we take too long, those assassin
pirates are gonna show up too. What?

48
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:08,780
Where'd he disappear to
I'm sure he went this way.

49
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,760
He's gotta be around here.

50
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:13,440
Okay, you guys look over there, right?

51
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:25,820
Hell is going on are they
chasing me I don't understand?

52
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:36,797
Wait a sec is this why
everyone's chasing after

53
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:39,577
me culprits in the
assassination plot well that

54
00:04:39,660 --> 00:04:42,097
Sucks can't go back to
the inn now I'll be out in

55
00:04:42,180 --> 00:04:46,317
the open hey who goes there
who are you over here?

56
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:49,197
There's a suspicious guy
hiding in the alley you

57
00:04:49,280 --> 00:04:51,837
sure about this there's
no mistake I'm certain.

58
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:55,257
They've been staying here at the inn
since they checked in last night.

59
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:57,497
They took off just a little while ago.

60
00:04:57,580 --> 00:04:58,797
They're staying here?

61
00:04:58,880 --> 00:04:59,917
Yes, that's right.

62
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,537
They still have lots of
luggage left in their room.

63
00:05:02,620 --> 00:05:05,032
I'm sure they'll be back for it sometime.

64
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:06,590
Right.

65
00:05:06,673 --> 00:05:08,071
You guys stay here, okay?

66
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:11,177
The rest of you search the
surrounding area with me.

67
00:05:11,260 --> 00:05:12,090
Look sharp.

68
00:05:12,173 --> 00:05:13,377
Leave no stone unturned.

69
00:05:13,460 --> 00:05:14,754
Does everybody got it?

70
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:27,690
Huh.

71
00:05:27,773 --> 00:05:28,603
No one's here.

72
00:05:29,140 --> 00:05:32,260
Are you 100 % certain
that this is their ship?

73
00:05:32,380 --> 00:05:33,717
There's no mistaking it.

74
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:34,630
Look up there.

75
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:37,077
That's the flag of the Straw Hat Pirates.

76
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:39,340
They probably already abandoned her.

77
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:41,900
She's all worn out.

78
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:47,600
Did you find them?

79
00:05:47,940 --> 00:05:49,120
No, they're gone.

80
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:51,217
There's not much left on board.

81
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:53,817
Pretty sure she was
abandoned and left to sink.

82
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:55,429
Let's keep looking around.

83
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:08,880
Who were those guys?

84
00:06:12,940 --> 00:06:15,293
Is there something going on in the city?

85
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:18,160
Find anything?

86
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:19,417
Not a trace of them.

87
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:20,330
Damn it!

88
00:06:20,413 --> 00:06:21,243
Where are they?

89
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:26,400
They sure are persistent.

90
00:06:26,980 --> 00:06:28,280
Hey, Luffy?

91
00:06:28,920 --> 00:06:29,750
Huh?

92
00:06:29,833 --> 00:06:30,720
What is it, Nami?

93
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:32,665
Do you think everybody's okay?

94
00:06:32,880 --> 00:06:34,880
These guys are all over the place.

95
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:39,897
Chopper and Sanji are probably safe because
no one knows their faces yet, but still.

96
00:06:39,980 --> 00:06:41,509
Come on, we need to hurry.

97
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:42,430
Right.

98
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:48,725
It looks like the C-Train's
still in operation.

99
00:06:49,340 --> 00:06:51,928
I guess the noon departure
has already left.

100
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:55,837
There's another one scheduled for
tonight, even in all this bad weather.

101
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:58,520
The 11 p .m., leaving for Annie's lobby.

102
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:01,217
That Sea Train is pretty impressive.

103
00:07:01,300 --> 00:07:03,097
Hey, any news on those pirates?

104
00:07:03,180 --> 00:07:04,239
We've got nothing.

105
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:07,817
If we can capture just one of those
three from the wanted posters,

106
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:09,757
we'll make them cough
up who the others are.

107
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:12,016
Hurry, before the waves get too high.

108
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:16,411
Maybe we can't find Robin
because she got on the Sea Train.

109
00:07:16,660 --> 00:07:20,717
Well, if she did, that would make
things worse than they already are.

110
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:23,506
Water 7's too big an
area to cover on its own.

111
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:25,150
What if...

112
00:07:25,233 --> 00:07:27,937
what if I did something to
upset her back at the bookstore?

113
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:28,850
Don't be ridiculous.

114
00:07:28,933 --> 00:07:30,351
No way that's the reason.

115
00:07:30,460 --> 00:07:31,480
Hey, excuse me.

116
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:34,177
Have you seen a beautiful woman
who kind of looks like this?

117
00:07:34,260 --> 00:07:36,777
You mean the one who's about 20
years older than that picture?

118
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:40,997
If I had, I would have told the newspapers
or the galley law company about it.

119
00:07:41,080 --> 00:07:42,780
To think she's an assassin.

120
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:44,514
Kind of shocking, huh?

121
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:46,250
Huh?

122
00:07:46,333 --> 00:07:48,017
I admire you for trying to
track down that criminal,

123
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:50,577
but I suggest you find
yourself some shelter soon.

124
00:07:50,660 --> 00:07:54,300
Aqua Laguna is on its
way. Ha ha ha. Take care.

125
00:08:00,340 --> 00:08:02,752
Things are getting dangerous around here.

126
00:08:02,980 --> 00:08:04,274
What about the others?

127
00:08:04,460 --> 00:08:05,517
Think they're okay?

128
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:07,020
I'm sure Luffy's fine.

129
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:10,595
Nami's the one that I'm really
worried about right now.

130
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:14,455
At any rate, this city's
becoming quite the ghost town.

131
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:17,237
The wind's really picking up.

132
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:20,144
I'm sure most people are
already in the shelter.

133
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:22,320
Where could she be?

134
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:25,137
Hey, Robin!

135
00:08:25,220 --> 00:08:26,400
Where are you?

136
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:31,420
That scent, is it...

137
00:08:33,560 --> 00:08:34,390
Huh?

138
00:08:34,580 --> 00:08:37,300
Chopper, what is it? Chopper!

139
00:08:39,620 --> 00:08:41,540
Hey, wait for me!

140
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:44,770
This way.

141
00:08:47,380 --> 00:08:49,280
Hey, Chopper! Chopper!

142
00:08:55,560 --> 00:08:56,760
Are you all right?

143
00:08:58,200 --> 00:09:00,024
Chopper, did you hurt yourself?

144
00:09:01,380 --> 00:09:02,460
There you are.

145
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:04,857
You can't just go running off like that.

146
00:09:04,940 --> 00:09:06,657
What the hell's the matter with you?

147
00:09:06,740 --> 00:09:09,960
One second, you're right beside me.

148
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:13,480
It's Robin!

149
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:15,970
Robin!

150
00:09:16,140 --> 00:09:17,677
Where in the world have you been?

151
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:18,878
Everyone's worried.

152
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:20,897
We've been looking everywhere for you.

153
00:09:20,980 --> 00:09:23,098
Come on, let's head back to the inn.

154
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:24,817
A lot's happened while you were gone.

155
00:09:24,900 --> 00:09:26,677
I'll explain everything on the way.

156
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:28,500
This damn water split us up.

157
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:30,030
Hold on.

158
00:09:30,113 --> 00:09:32,120
I'll find another way over there.

159
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:35,200
Don't bother. It's all right.

160
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:36,740
Stay where you are.

161
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:39,380
There's no need.

162
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,257
Indeed, because I won't be
coming back to you and your crew.

163
00:09:43,340 --> 00:09:46,860
We're parting ways, here, in this city.

164
00:09:47,660 --> 00:09:48,490
What the...

165
00:09:48,573 --> 00:09:50,913
what in the world are you talking about?

166
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:54,477
Oh, wait, you mean the stuff they
said about you in the newspaper?

167
00:09:54,560 --> 00:09:55,795
Don't worry about it.

168
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:57,413
None of us believes it.

169
00:09:57,520 --> 00:10:00,097
Pirates are falsely accused
of crimes all the time.

170
00:10:00,180 --> 00:10:01,298
We're easy targets.

171
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:03,550
About that.

172
00:10:03,633 --> 00:10:07,344
I apologize for pinning such an
unreasonable crime on all of you.

173
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:12,117
But as far as my involvement, everything
that was said in the newspaper is true.

174
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:16,553
Late last night, I broke into the
mayor's place of residence and shot him.

175
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:18,680
No way.

176
00:10:19,840 --> 00:10:23,260
Inside me, I carry a darkness
that none of you know about.

177
00:10:24,060 --> 00:10:27,760
One day, that darkness will
be the end of all of you.

178
00:10:28,940 --> 00:10:31,257
Every organization that
she's had something

179
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:33,797
to do with in the past
has been annihilated.

180
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:37,800
Not one single solitary
member escaped except for her.

181
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:42,317
I'm afraid you'll be taking the fall
for last night's attack while I escape.

182
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:46,420
And let me warn you, the
situation will only get worse.

183
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:47,917
What are you talking about?

184
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,118
I don't understand!

185
00:10:49,380 --> 00:10:52,674
Why I'm doing it, there's no
need for you to understand.

186
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:55,990
Robin!

187
00:10:56,073 --> 00:10:56,903
What happened?

188
00:10:56,986 --> 00:10:58,137
You're not making any sense!

189
00:10:58,220 --> 00:10:59,657
This isn't like you at all!

190
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:00,570
Please!

191
00:11:00,653 --> 00:11:02,166
We'll work this out together!

192
00:11:03,880 --> 00:11:07,821
Although I only spent a short time
with you, from this day forward,

193
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:10,520
we will never see each other again.

194
00:11:11,740 --> 00:11:14,477
Thank you for all of the
kindness you've shown me.

195
00:11:14,560 --> 00:11:16,384
Know that I'll never forget it.

196
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:18,650
Goodbye.

197
00:11:35,780 --> 00:11:36,617
Wait!

198
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:37,620
No!

199
00:11:38,080 --> 00:11:38,910
Please!

200
00:11:38,993 --> 00:11:40,577
This can't...

201
00:11:40,660 --> 00:11:43,120
This can't be happening!

202
00:11:46,440 --> 00:11:47,277
Hey!

203
00:11:47,360 --> 00:11:48,740
Come back!

204
00:11:52,360 --> 00:11:53,280
Stop!

205
00:11:53,740 --> 00:11:56,340
You don't know what you're saying, Robin!

206
00:11:57,080 --> 00:11:59,860
Wait! Please! Come back!

207
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:20,000
I lost track of her scent. I see.

208
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:24,540
Hey, Chopper.

209
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:28,257
Go meet up with Luffy
and the others and tell

210
00:12:28,340 --> 00:12:30,937
them everything that happened
between us and Robin.

211
00:12:31,020 --> 00:12:33,608
I don't want you to
leave out a single word.

212
00:12:34,140 --> 00:12:34,970
Sure.

213
00:12:35,053 --> 00:12:37,660
As for me, let's just say I have a plan.

214
00:12:38,540 --> 00:12:40,200
I'll try to be careful.

215
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:41,776
We'll meet up later.

216
00:12:43,920 --> 00:12:44,861
Where'd they go?

217
00:12:45,180 --> 00:12:46,540
Check the alleys!

218
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:50,944
You don't think they're
on the rooftops, do you?

219
00:12:51,060 --> 00:12:52,500
Damn it, we lost them!

220
00:12:53,040 --> 00:12:54,100
I don't get it.

221
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:55,717
I'm sure they went this way.

222
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:57,094
We better keep moving.

223
00:12:57,420 --> 00:12:59,677
All right, but we should check
inside the buildings, too.

224
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:00,590
Good!

225
00:13:00,673 --> 00:13:01,503
We'll split up.

226
00:13:01,586 --> 00:13:02,540
Let's go! Yeah!

227
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:07,540
Is it okay now? Wait a sec.

228
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:11,227
Where did you last see them?

229
00:13:14,020 --> 00:13:15,440
Just a little longer.

230
00:13:27,360 --> 00:13:28,190
Hmm?

231
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,200
What? Stop!

232
00:13:39,240 --> 00:13:40,540
I'm begging you.

233
00:13:41,260 --> 00:13:42,500
Are you crazy?

234
00:13:42,820 --> 00:13:43,879
I got to evacuate.

235
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:45,200
Stop pestering me.

236
00:13:45,960 --> 00:13:46,790
Come on.

237
00:13:47,220 --> 00:13:48,580
I have money, okay?

238
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:51,200
Here, take it.

239
00:13:51,420 --> 00:13:54,596
I need as much lumber, tar,
and rope as this will buy.

240
00:13:54,780 --> 00:13:58,337
Oh, and also some nails, latches,
and tin plates, if you don't mind.

241
00:13:58,420 --> 00:14:00,200
I said I'm closing the shop.

242
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:02,500
It'll just take a second. Please.

243
00:14:08,780 --> 00:14:12,477
Okay, kid, but I'm afraid this
money ain't gonna buy much for you.

244
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:15,520
Uh, then how about I sell my tools?

245
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:17,097
Will that make up for the rest?

246
00:14:17,180 --> 00:14:19,360
Hey, hey, come on, stop it.

247
00:14:19,540 --> 00:14:20,840
We don't do barter.

248
00:14:21,020 --> 00:14:22,537
This is the big city, you know.

249
00:14:22,620 --> 00:14:24,460
I'm sorry, but it's cash only.

250
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:30,280
You win, but let's make it quick.

251
00:14:38,020 --> 00:14:40,517
You sure you're okay
carrying that with all those

252
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:44,277
injuries can't you get some
friends to help you out?

253
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:49,240
Hey I knew this was a bad idea!

254
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:08,240
Wait this isn't gonna work.

255
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:10,037
I'm fine.

256
00:15:10,120 --> 00:15:11,297
I got it.

257
00:15:11,380 --> 00:15:12,497
This is nothing.

258
00:15:12,580 --> 00:15:16,217
Don't worry I can do it. No look.

259
00:15:16,300 --> 00:15:18,137
Here take these.

260
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:19,640
You're hungry, right?

261
00:15:24,700 --> 00:15:25,577
Thank you.

262
00:15:25,660 --> 00:15:26,800
Sure thing!

263
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:28,740
Try to be careful.

264
00:15:35,500 --> 00:15:37,260
Good luck out there, kid.

265
00:15:45,780 --> 00:15:46,610
Mmm.

266
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:49,200
These are good.

267
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,020
Really good.

268
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,500
Guess that guy was pretty nice after all.

269
00:16:08,500 --> 00:16:11,147
The waves sure are
getting high, aren't they?

270
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:18,520
Don't worry, Mary.

271
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:20,606
You're going to be just fine.

272
00:16:28,740 --> 00:16:32,440
After all, you flew in the sky, remember?

273
00:16:33,740 --> 00:16:35,920
You got nothing to be afraid of.

274
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:46,740
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

275
00:16:47,280 --> 00:16:49,560
What's got you riled up, big guy?

276
00:16:57,640 --> 00:16:59,920
Come on, Franky, you can tell us.

277
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:08,442
What's up, bro?

278
00:17:10,020 --> 00:17:14,667
I got so much rage inside me, I feel
another rampage coming on right about now!

279
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:18,029
Hey, wait for me, bro,
don't rampage alone!

280
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:21,972
As always, thanks for the drinks, Blueno!

281
00:17:25,660 --> 00:17:27,577
What got into him all of a sudden?

282
00:17:27,660 --> 00:17:29,307
Is there something going on?

283
00:17:33,340 --> 00:17:34,170
It's me.

284
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:36,606
Never can tell with that guy.

285
00:17:36,900 --> 00:17:39,400
Only idiots know what idiots are thinking.

286
00:17:52,380 --> 00:17:54,097
Looks like the crowd cleared out.

287
00:17:54,180 --> 00:17:55,477
Yeah, no thanks to you.

288
00:17:55,560 --> 00:17:59,037
I'll have you know that Luffy and I
had a perfectly good hiding place.

289
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:01,617
Until you led that angry
mob straight to us.

290
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:03,517
Like I said, with that
many people looking.

291
00:18:03,600 --> 00:18:04,857
They were going to find you anyway.

292
00:18:04,940 --> 00:18:07,037
Oh yeah, that reminds me.

293
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:09,237
How'd you know we were
down there, Chopper?

294
00:18:09,320 --> 00:18:10,150
Your smell?

295
00:18:10,600 --> 00:18:14,180
Ah, should have known But
wait, wasn't Sanji with you?

296
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:16,080
Well, he was

297
00:18:30,060 --> 00:18:30,940
No way!

298
00:18:31,100 --> 00:18:32,497
That doesn't make any sense!

299
00:18:32,580 --> 00:18:34,521
Did Robin really say that to you?

300
00:18:42,520 --> 00:18:44,880
We were prepared for this, weren't we?

301
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:52,100
After all, Robin was our enemy
before we let her join the crew.

302
00:18:52,480 --> 00:18:57,068
This might be our only chance to find
out the truth, so we shouldn't run away.

303
00:18:59,240 --> 00:19:02,534
There's still a lot of things
we don't know about Robin.

304
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:07,300
Now it's time to decide if
she's a friend or a foe.

305
00:19:09,860 --> 00:19:12,020
The situation will get worse.

306
00:19:12,300 --> 00:19:15,960
From this day forward, we
will never see each other.

307
00:19:21,980 --> 00:19:22,810
You're sure?

308
00:19:22,893 --> 00:19:24,506
That's all she said, Chopper?

309
00:19:27,520 --> 00:19:31,577
If she says she won't see us after
today and things are gonna get worse,

310
00:19:31,660 --> 00:19:34,277
maybe that means the attack
on Iceberg was just a warm

311
00:19:34,360 --> 00:19:37,772
-up and she has something even
bigger planned for tonight.

312
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:43,557
I don't know why Robin's
doing any of this,

313
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:46,017
so it's hard to make a guess
as to what she's planning!

314
00:19:46,100 --> 00:19:49,717
But seeing how much commotion her
first attack on the mayor caused,

315
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:55,020
there's only one way to make things
worse in other words she'll murder him

316
00:19:58,200 --> 00:20:01,259
I think that's what she's
trying to tell us at least

317
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:05,777
Also since she told Chopper that
she'll be pinning the crime on us,

318
00:20:05,860 --> 00:20:07,737
it could be that she's
feeding us all these little

319
00:20:07,820 --> 00:20:10,977
hints to try and lure us out
to the crime scene tonight?

320
00:20:11,060 --> 00:20:11,890
Think so?

321
00:20:12,220 --> 00:20:16,197
If that is her plan, it would be convenient
for her if we did happen to show up,

322
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:18,597
since that would put us
at the scene of the crime.

323
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:20,237
You say you don't know
what she's thinking,

324
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:23,517
but it sounds to me like you've
already decided that she's our enemy.

325
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:25,917
I'm talking about
possibilities here, that's all.

326
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,457
We should always be prepared for
the worst-case scenario, understand?

327
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:33,337
If I get locked into a single line
of thinking, it'll only slow me down.

328
00:20:33,420 --> 00:20:36,361
If she's my friend, I have
to be ready to forgive.

329
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:40,000
But if she's my enemy, I
have to be ready to fight.

330
00:20:44,420 --> 00:20:49,160
Our best chance to settle this is
tonight are we going of course?

331
00:20:50,700 --> 00:20:53,917
It's not that I object
to the plan but we're

332
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:57,217
still forgetting something
Sanji said he saw.

333
00:20:57,300 --> 00:20:59,597
Robin walking with
someone in a mask remember

334
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:03,497
obviously that wasn't one of
us but Iceberg said exactly

335
00:21:03,580 --> 00:21:06,037
the same thing that he
was attacked by Robin and

336
00:21:06,120 --> 00:21:08,457
a large man in a mask
that he didn't recognize.

337
00:21:08,540 --> 00:21:13,097
Whoever he is I bet he's the reason
Robin is doing all of this stuff.

338
00:21:13,180 --> 00:21:15,517
Yeah that means it isn't our
fault and we just need to

339
00:21:15,600 --> 00:21:18,697
beat the real bad guy right
that's the ideal situation.

340
00:21:18,780 --> 00:21:23,197
But on the other hand it's also possible
that this guy is one of Robin's friends.

341
00:21:23,280 --> 00:21:27,537
The problem is we don't have much to
go on other than a big man in a mask.

342
00:21:27,620 --> 00:21:31,977
So where do we even start I mean
what is our goal here we find

343
00:21:32,060 --> 00:21:36,860
Robin and capture her that's the
only way we'll ever know the truth.

344
00:21:38,340 --> 00:21:41,987
You're right, we're wasting time
here trying to figure it out.

345
00:21:42,600 --> 00:21:45,247
Just one thing, Robin
won't be easy to catch.

346
00:21:45,560 --> 00:21:46,390
After all,

347
00:21:46,473 --> 00:21:50,857
the world government's been trying for
20 years and it still hasn't happened.

348
00:21:50,940 --> 00:21:54,411
Like he said, it's the only
way we'll really know for sure.

349
00:21:55,720 --> 00:21:57,720
Yeah, let's settle this right now!

350
00:21:58,380 --> 00:21:59,210
Right.

351
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:01,760
Come on, Galilaw's waiting.

352
00:22:08,460 --> 00:22:09,640
Damn, it's late.

353
00:22:09,800 --> 00:22:11,800
Where'd that Straw Hat run off to?

354
00:22:12,120 --> 00:22:13,880
Paulie, we gotta go.

355
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:16,906
All these streets are
gonna flood before long.

356
00:22:17,160 --> 00:22:18,760
All right, let's head back.

357
00:22:19,120 --> 00:22:20,826
I'm going to the main office.

358
00:22:21,600 --> 00:22:22,497
Sounds good, boss.

359
00:22:22,580 --> 00:22:23,756
You heard him, guys.

360
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:24,880
Time to move out.

361
00:22:28,060 --> 00:22:31,817
Get out here and find me, Straw Hat!

362
00:22:31,900 --> 00:22:33,157
Where are you?

363
00:22:33,240 --> 00:22:34,420
Stop hiding!

364
00:22:36,180 --> 00:22:40,298
I thought that little turd had some
backbone, but I guess I was wrong.

365
00:22:41,140 --> 00:22:42,740
Won't even show his face.

366
00:22:43,320 --> 00:22:44,537
I know what you're saying,

367
00:22:44,620 --> 00:22:48,177
bro, but to be fair, the whole island
is hunting him down right now, you know?

368
00:22:48,260 --> 00:22:49,090
Exactly.

369
00:22:49,173 --> 00:22:52,040
I bet he's hiding if he
hasn't been caught already.

370
00:22:52,400 --> 00:22:55,597
By the way, what's with this weird
crab walk thing all of a sudden?

371
00:22:55,680 --> 00:22:59,920
If we face the front, then the wind
catches our hair, and we blow away!

372
00:23:01,440 --> 00:23:05,097
Speaking of which, the weather isn't the
only thing that's out of control today.

373
00:23:05,180 --> 00:23:06,010
Tell me about it.

374
00:23:06,093 --> 00:23:08,877
It's like you've got a rampage
going on inside you, too.

375
00:23:08,960 --> 00:23:09,790
Shut up.

376
00:23:09,960 --> 00:23:12,019
I'm just like that this week, okay?

377
00:23:12,940 --> 00:23:14,240
Hey, Ro!

378
00:23:14,820 --> 00:23:16,257
Hey, it's Ro! Hey, Ro!

379
00:23:16,340 --> 00:23:17,869
Well, if it isn't, Samba.

380
00:23:19,220 --> 00:23:20,050
Tell me!

381
00:23:20,133 --> 00:23:22,497
Tell me that you beat up
those stupid Straw Hats!

382
00:23:22,580 --> 00:23:23,717
Yeah, but I tried to.

383
00:23:23,800 --> 00:23:27,506
Some angry mops showed up, got
in the way, then Luffy took off.

384
00:23:28,140 --> 00:23:29,980
Are those guys lucky or what?

385
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:32,871
When you're on a rampage, nobody survives.

386
00:23:33,320 --> 00:23:34,150
That's weird.

387
00:23:34,260 --> 00:23:37,717
I wondered why that weak dude with the
long nose was fixing the ship on his own.

388
00:23:37,800 --> 00:23:39,997
I figured that you'd wrecked
up the rest of the crew so

389
00:23:40,080 --> 00:23:43,077
bad that he was the only one
left who could do anything.

390
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:45,140
Wait, you found one of them?

391
00:23:45,780 --> 00:23:47,540
Yeah, on their ship.

392
00:23:51,780 --> 00:23:54,780
Well, that's just fine,
because all we need is one.

393
00:23:54,880 --> 00:23:59,233
In other words, we'll use that loser
as bait to lure out the rest of them.

394
00:23:59,460 --> 00:24:02,160
Whoa, bro's got his bad guy face on, guys!

395
00:24:03,820 --> 00:24:05,757
All right, you good-for-nuffins.

396
00:24:05,840 --> 00:24:09,177
I want you to march through the
town and spread the word for me.

397
00:24:09,260 --> 00:24:13,477
Say, we've got Longnose, and if you
don't want him swimming with the fishes?

398
00:24:13,560 --> 00:24:15,777
then come to the warehouse
under the bridge.

399
00:24:15,860 --> 00:24:18,840
Tell him Franky sent ya.

400
00:24:21,780 --> 00:24:26,427
In the meantime, I'll go nab Longnose so
we can make good on our little threat.

401
00:24:26,740 --> 00:24:27,960
You get it, bro!

402
00:24:28,160 --> 00:24:30,000
I swear we won't let you down!

403
00:24:49,340 --> 00:24:52,020
Aqua Laguna is coming for you!

404
00:24:52,480 --> 00:24:54,460
Here comes a big wave!

405
00:24:56,320 --> 00:24:59,277
So, do you know what's going
on with those Straw Hats?

406
00:24:59,360 --> 00:25:00,190
I'm not sure.

407
00:25:00,273 --> 00:25:02,217
I don't think they've caught them yet.

408
00:25:02,300 --> 00:25:03,500
Still on the loose.

409
00:25:04,340 --> 00:25:05,340
That's no good.

410
00:25:05,580 --> 00:25:08,177
And with everyone so
worked up about the storm,

411
00:25:08,260 --> 00:25:11,084
they'll have the perfect
chance to attack again.

412
00:25:13,060 --> 00:25:15,001
And what I heard is that tonight?

413
00:25:15,180 --> 00:25:17,137
All the craftsmen from
the Call Law Company.

414
00:25:17,220 --> 00:25:19,757
and he will be guarding the main
office to protect the mayor.

415
00:25:19,840 --> 00:25:20,670
Whoa!

416
00:25:20,753 --> 00:25:22,519
That's a really big deal, isn't it?

417
00:25:23,060 --> 00:25:25,657
How many people have the
Straw Hats got, anyway?

418
00:25:25,740 --> 00:25:29,100
Some say 50, some say 100, or even more!

419
00:25:29,420 --> 00:25:32,677
Remember, the captain's got
100 million bounty on his head.

420
00:25:32,760 --> 00:25:33,737
For all we know,

421
00:25:33,820 --> 00:25:38,017
he could be sending an army of 3,000 men
to fight the shipwrights as we speak!

422
00:25:38,100 --> 00:25:38,957
Are you kidding?

423
00:25:39,040 --> 00:25:40,440
That sounds really bad!

424
00:25:42,660 --> 00:25:44,640
What are we gonna do?

425
00:25:46,460 --> 00:25:51,240
All right, men, hold your formation
and don't give an inch. Yeah!

426
00:25:52,280 --> 00:25:55,560
Don't even let a single fly
get through, got it? Yeah!

427
00:26:13,100 --> 00:26:14,500
Bring it on!

428
00:26:16,540 --> 00:26:17,840
What's wrong with you?

429
00:26:18,300 --> 00:26:20,535
Would you please be quiet, Tile Stone?

430
00:26:21,660 --> 00:26:24,657
I heard the Straw Hats weren't
spotted on the Sea Train.

431
00:26:24,740 --> 00:26:27,916
That means they're still
here on the island somewhere.

432
00:26:28,800 --> 00:26:29,630
Still,

433
00:26:29,713 --> 00:26:33,077
they'd be complete idiots if they tried to
show up with all of these guards around.

434
00:26:33,160 --> 00:26:37,097
Yeah, you'd think, but that didn't stop
the dumbass that barged in here earlier,

435
00:26:37,180 --> 00:26:38,010
did it?

436
00:26:38,840 --> 00:26:40,800
We gotta be ready for anything.

437
00:26:42,520 --> 00:26:45,700
Well, this is reassuring,
but it's a bit much.

438
00:26:46,260 --> 00:26:48,200
They wanted to do this for you.

439
00:26:49,140 --> 00:26:50,460
I'm not royalty.

440
00:26:50,980 --> 00:26:51,857
Pardon me, sir,

441
00:26:51,940 --> 00:26:56,175
but why on earth did you put Nico
Robin's wanted poster up on your wall?

442
00:26:56,420 --> 00:26:57,480
It bother you?

443
00:26:59,760 --> 00:27:00,720
A bit.

444
00:27:04,800 --> 00:27:06,565
It's better if you don't know.

445
00:27:10,500 --> 00:27:13,020
That girl is a demon.

446
00:27:40,780 --> 00:27:43,192
There sure are a lot of people out there.

447
00:27:43,380 --> 00:27:44,733
It's a little far, too.

448
00:27:44,860 --> 00:27:47,237
It'll be fine if you rocket
through the window, right?

449
00:27:47,320 --> 00:27:48,997
After Robin shows up, I mean.

450
00:27:49,080 --> 00:27:49,910
That's right.

451
00:27:49,993 --> 00:27:51,397
If we make a commotion first,

452
00:27:51,480 --> 00:27:53,737
then they'll just sneak in while
we're dealing with the guards.

453
00:27:53,820 --> 00:27:54,820
Let's be patient.

454
00:27:55,240 --> 00:27:56,180
Get ready!

455
00:27:56,540 --> 00:28:00,220
Strike at anything that
moves, men! Got it? Yeah!
